---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Creating and Managing Banners">
  <div class="docs-content">
    <h1>Creating and Managing Banners</h1>

    <h2>Banner Editor Interface</h2>
    <p>When entering the editing mode of a banner, you'll see:</p>

    <h3>1. Header Information - Left Side</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Banner title</li>
      <li>Auto-save indicator (changes save automatically)</li>
      <li>Last edited timestamp</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>2. Header Publishing - Right Side</h3>
    <p><strong>Publish/Unpublish button</strong> - Control banner visibility on your store</p>
    <ul>
      <li><p>The Publish button will show if your latest changes are published</p></li>
      <li>The status is <strong>Unpublished</strong></li>
      <ul>
        <li>There are recent changes that were not published</li>
        <li>Press the button to publish the latest changes</li>
      </ul>
      <li>The status is <strong>Published</strong></li>
      <ul>
        <li>Your banner is published with the latest changes</li>
        <li>Press the button if you want to unpublish it</li>
      </ul>
    </ul>

    <h3>3. Status Output Bar</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>The Status Output Bar shows the information about the status of your banner and useful instructions are displayed</li>
      <li>Take into consideration the displayed information and use it to make the necessary adjustments</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>4. Preview Navigation</h3>
    <p><strong>Preview modes</strong> - Test your banner in different responsive views:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Large mode</li>
      <ul>
        <li>Usually matches Desktop devices</li>
      </ul>
      <li>Medium mode</li>
      <ul>
        <li>Usually matches Tablet devices</li>
      </ul>
      <li>Small mode</li>
      <ul>
        <li>Usually matches Mobile devices</li>
      </ul>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Navigation controls</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Use the arrows (left/right) to navigate between slides</li>
      <li>Use navigation dots shown below the preview for quick access to specific slides</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="docs-tip">
      <p><strong>Best Practice:</strong> Use the three responsive modes to test your banners across all devices to ensure they look great on every device, but also check the actual devices when possible for the most accurate results.</p>
    </div>

    <hr />

    <div class="mt-12 flex gap-4">
      <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/docs/dashboard`} class="btn bg-gray-200 text-gray-700 hover:bg-gray-300">
        ← Previous: Main Dashboard
      </a>
      <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/docs/slide-types`} class="btn btn-primary">
        Next: Slide Types →
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
